<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Monochrome layer for Android's themed icons (Android 13+).

  Draw the glyph in a SINGLE colour and let the launcher tint it - that is what makes the icon
  follow the user's theme instead of fighting it. fillType="evenOdd" turns the key rectangles into
  holes in the keyboard body, so this is one silhouette rather than overlapping shapes, which is
  what a monochrome layer needs to render cleanly at small sizes.
-->
